In the diagram, point $F$ lies on line segment $CD$, and triangles $CFG$ and $DFH$ are isosceles. Also, $\angle FHG$ is twice $\angle DFC$. What is the measure of $\angle GFH$ in degrees?

[asy]
import olympiad;
import math;

size(7cm);

// Draw triangles
pair c = (-2 * Cos(50), 0);
pair d = (1, 0);
pair f = (0, 0);
pair g = dir(130);
pair h = dir(70);
draw(c--g--f--cycle);
draw(f--d--h--cycle);

// Labels
label("$C$", c, W); label("$D$", d, E);
label("$F$", f, S); label("$G$", g, N);
label("$H$", h, N); label("$50^\circ$", d, 2 * NW+ 0.5 * W);

// Ticks
add(pathticks(c--g, s=2));
add(pathticks(g--f, s=2));
add(pathticks(f--h, 2, spacing=0.7, s=2));
add(pathticks(f--d, 2, spacing=0.7, s=2));
[/asy]
